 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "Gold is the second component of India's foreign exchange reserves and represents gold coin and bullion held by the Reserve Bank in both the Issue Department and the Banking Department. RBI values this gold close to international market prices, revaluing it at the end of each month at 90 per cent of the daily average price quoted by the London Bullion Market Association, and publishes the resulting value weekly in the WSS. The published figure therefore moves with both the quantity of gold held and international gold prices — a rise does not necessarily mean the RBI bought gold.",
   "source_name": "RBI — A Handbook on RBI's Weekly Statistical Supplement: Concepts, Definitions and Methodologies",
   "source_url": "https://rbidocs.rbi.org.in/rdocs/Publications/PDFs/HWSSF170614.pdf",
